Examples for the ILVES bond/angle constraint solver.
Example input files:
  in.peptide-fast     -- peptide + water with ilves, symmetric variant (fast)
  in.peptide-full     -- peptide + water with ilves, exact-Newton variant (full)
  in.peptide-mix      -- peptide groups via ilves, water via fix shake
  in.peptide-allbonds -- ilves constraining ALL bonds, demonstrating
                         arbitrarily-large connected bonds cluster support
  in.peptide-shake    -- baseline using fix shake for comparison
  in.peptide-rattle   -- baseline using fix rattle for comparison
  in.rhodo-full       -- rhodopsin with C-H bonds + H-O-H water angle (full)
  in.rhodo-fast       -- rhodopsin with same constraints (fast)
  in.rhodo-allbonds   -- rhodopsin with all bonds + water angle increased comm cutoff
  in.bulk_co2         -- bulk CO2 fluid (rigid linear; see comments in manual
                         for caveats on exactly-180 deg symmetric angles)
  in.cg-polymers      -- coarse-grain polymer chains with 180 deg backbone angles
